@startuml sequence-submission-email
' Spec 004 — an Employer's submission and the email to the Admins (REQ-004-10; REQ-003-6, -8).
' Parties: Employer's browser, JairojobsWeb (Employer listing LiveView), Jairojobs.Listings, Postgres,
' Mailer (Resend in production), each Admin's inbox.

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Employer
participant "Browser" as B
participant "JairojobsWeb\n(Employer.ListingLive.Show)" as W
participant "Jairojobs.Listings" as L
database "Postgres" as DB
participant "ListingNotifier\n+ Jairojobs.Mailer" as M
participant "Resend" as R
participant "Admins' inboxes" as IN

Employer -> B : Submit for approval (or Resubmit)
B -> W : event
W -> L : submit_listing(scope, listing, admin_url)

group one transaction (the checks of spec 003)
  L -> DB : lock the owner row and the listing row,\ncheck status, completeness, region, limit
  alt a check fails
    L --> W : {:error, reason}
    W --> B : message, as in spec 003
  else passes
    L -> DB : status → pending, submitted_at,\nclear the previous decision
    DB --> L : committed
  end
end

note over L, DB : The submission is saved and committed\nbefore any email is attempted.

L -> DB : Admin accounts, except the submitter
loop each Admin
  L -> M : deliver_submitted(admin, listing, url)
  M -> R : send
  alt accepted
    R -> IN : "A listing is waiting for approval: <title>"
  else refused, unreachable, or raises
    L -> L : log the kind of email\nand the listing id, nothing else
  end
end
L --> W : {:ok, listing}
W --> B : "Submitted. An admin will check it\nbefore it goes live."

note over B, IN
  The Employer never sees an email failure. The listing is in the queue
  and counted on the Admin area either way. A withdrawal sends nothing.
end note
@enduml
